# Shell scripts are run on Linux (the Android build) and on macOS; a CRLF in them is a "bad
# interpreter" or a stray $'\r'. Keep them LF wherever they are checked out, and keep the Windows
# scripts CRLF, which is what cmd.exe and PowerShell expect.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Assets and archives are binaries; never touch their line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.so binary
